/-!
# Openness of the normal crossing locus (Ch. 0 §5, Def. 2; Ch. IV §1, Lemma 1)

The set of points of `D` at which `E` has only normal crossings with `D` is open in `D`.  This is the
last step of the proof of Lemma 1 of Ch. IV §1 (p. 277), which is proved here as printed:

> All left to be proved is that, if `W` has only normal crossings with `⋃_{i=1}^α E_i` at a point `x`
> of `W`, then there exists an open subset of `W` containing `x` at every point of which `W` has only
> normal crossings with `⋃_{i=1}^α E_i`. … we may assume that:
> (1) For every subsystem `(z_{i₁}, …, z_{i_t})` of `(z_{s+1}, …, z_r)`,
> `(z₁, …, z_s, z_{i₁}, …, z_{i_t})A` is a prime ideal in `A`, and
> `A/(z₁, …, z_s, z_{i₁}, …, z_{i_t})A` is a regular ring, and,
> (2) `Spec(A) ∩ W` is irreducible (hence, non-singular by (1)), so that `(z₁, …, z_s)A` is the prime
> ideal of `W` in the affine ring `A`, and
> (3) `Spec(A)` has empty intersection with any of the `E_j` which does not pass through `x`. …

(Proof of Lemma 1, p. 277, abridged here: the statement and the conditions (1)–(3), with the
omitted steps discussed one by one below.)  The Lean proof follows the full printed text, in this
order; the paper-form statement (`W` reduced, `E` reduced
everywhere of codimension one) is `exists_isOpen_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_of_isReduced`, and
the lemma for arbitrary `E`, `D` (`exists_isOpen_hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt`) differs from it only
in (2).

* "Let `Spec(A)` be an affine open subscheme of `X` which contains the given point `x`": an affine
  open `V₀ ∋ x`, `A₀ = Γ(X, V₀)`, of finite type over a base ring `S ∈ 𝔅`; `P` is the prime `p`
  of `x` in `A₀`, `A₀_p = O_{X,x}` (`IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_stalk`).
* "We have a regular system of parameters `(z₁, …, z_r)` of `A_P`": the hypothesis of Def. 2, `z`,
  with `t ⊆ z` generating the ideal of `D` at `x` (the paper's `W`, `(z₁, …, z_s)`); the ideals of the
  components of `E` through `x` are generated by members of `z`.  The `z_j` are elements of `A_P`,
  while (1) speaks of ideals of `A` generated by them: Lean takes representatives `f a ∈ A₀` with
  `f a` associated to `a` in `A_P` (gap filled, see the end).
* "By replacing `A` by `A_f` with a suitable `f ∈ A − P`" (`exists_isAffineOpen_prime_system`): each
  of the finitely many conditions below holds on a neighbourhood of `p` in `Spec A₀`; a basic open
  `D(f₀) ∋ p` lies in all of them (`f₀ ∉ p`), and `A := Γ(X, D(f₀))` is `(A₀)_{f₀}`
  (`IsLocalization.Away f₀ A`), `Spec A = D(f₀)`.  The conditions, in the form needed to verify
  (1)–(3) for `A`:
  (1) for every subsystem `G` of `z ∖ t` the ideal `I_G = (t ∪ G)A₀` has the same localizations as the
  prime `𝔭_G = I_G A₀_p ∩ A₀` (finite generation: `eventually_map_le_map_of_map_le`), and
  `A₀/I_G` is regular on `D(f₀)` (the openness of the regular locus, (iii) of p. 161 — the only cited
  input, `eventually_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_map`); so `I_G A = 𝔭_G A` is a prime ideal of `A`
  (`IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint`) and `A/I_G A` is a regular ring (`IsRegularRing`);
  (2) the components of `D` not through `x` are avoided by `D(f₀)`, so every component of `D`
  meeting `Spec A` passes through `x` ("`Spec(A) ∩ W` is irreducible"); and the ideal of `D` on
  `D(f₀)` is `(z₁, …, z_s)A` (finite generation — used by the lemma for arbitrary `D` only);
  (3) the ideal of each component of `E` meeting `Spec A` is `(z_j)A` for a `z_j ∈ z` (finite
  generation; the components not through `x` are avoided by `D(f₀)`).
  Equalities of ideals of `A` are checked stalkwise (`map_eq_map_of_forall_germ`).
* (2) as printed, for `W` reduced (`ideal_eq_span_of_isReduced`): "`Spec(A) ∩ W` is irreducible (hence,
  non-singular by (1)), so that `(z₁, …, z_s)A` is the prime ideal of `W` in the affine ring `A`": the
  ideal of `W` in `A` is radical, its minimal primes are all `(z₁, …, z_s)A`, a prime by (1) for the
  empty subsystem having the same localization at `P`.
* "Now, if `y` is any point of `Spec(A) ∩ W` …": `hasOnlyNormalCrossingsWithAt_of_prime_system`,
  whose key step "by (1) the subsystem … can be extended to a regular system of parameters of the
  local ring `A_Q`" is `extendsToRSOP_image_of_isPrime`.

Gaps in the paper filled: (a) "by (1) … can be
extended" is a one-line claim; regularity of `A_Q/(subsystem)A_Q` alone does not suffice, the
height count `ht ≥ #subsystem` is needed and uses the primality in (1) (`le_height_of_isPrime_of_le_height_map`);
(b) the `z_j` are tacitly elements of `A`; (c) the ideal of each `E_j` through `x` in `A` is
`(z_j)A`, which the paper uses (in "by (2) and (3)") without listing it among (1)–(3); (d) that the
replacement of `A` by some `A_f` achieves (1)–(3) is not argued.
Deviation from the paper (statement modified), only in the lemma for arbitrary `E`, `D`: it is
stated for arbitrary subschemes of a non-singular algebraic scheme, not for `W` reduced and
`E = ⋃ E_j` reduced of codimension one; accordingly, in (2) the ideal of `D` in `A` is made equal to
`(z₁, …, z_s)A` by finite generation (`D` need not be reduced), in place of the paper's argument.
-/

